hroughput","body":"Context syncing no longer starts a full archive rebuild on every status poll while uploads keep changing the archive. Background builds wait for a quiet revision and share a bounded scheduler; explicit reads and cloud preparation retain their current authority and revision checks. Inbox presence, route leases and delivery receipts commit atomically, reducing repeated disk commits.\n\nServer-only follow-up to native 0.4.42/runtime75. No schema, sharing policy, classifier, auth, quota or durability changes. Exact tests, artifact hashes and deployment receipts are tracked in the source repository.\n"}